  "loot": "Owned ore loot retains native ordinary/Fortune/explosion formulas and uses owned Silk Touch block and random sequence IDs. Minecraft/Create loot schemas were adapted. Palladium uses the same standard ore schema as zinc with the existing Galosphere raw-palladium item; no Galosphere table is redistributed.",
  "client_acceptance": "Offline pixel identities and dimensions are checked separately from owner client atlas/model/shader acceptance.",
  "galosphere": "1.5.3",
  "galosphere_project": "https://modrinth.com/mod/galosphere/version/Y3deS8Po",
  "processing": "Smelting/blasting retain original material outputs and furnace experience. Nine existing Create deepslate-ore crushing routes retain their exact yields/chances/durations and use blackstone instead of cobbled deepslate byproduct. Palladium retains its existing drop/furnace routes; no new crushing route is invented.",
  "mining": "Native deepslate hardness/sound, tool tags, exact XP providers and XP random consumption are retained. Create zinc requires an iron-tier tool, matching its pinned needs_iron_tool tag. Galosphere deepslate palladium has requiresCorrectToolForDrops=false in its pinned artifact; its blackstone variant preserves that provider behavior."
